  "summary": "Building a malicious package that uses cgo could cause arbitrary code execution at build time through several compiler…",
  "details": "Building a malicious package that uses cgo could cause arbitrary code execution at build time through several compiler and linker flags permitted in \"#cgo\" directives. Specifically, \"--sysroot\" in GCC and Clang relocates compiler subprograms, spec files, and CRT startup objects to an attacker-controlled directory; \"-target\" in Clang falls back to executing target helper tools from the current working directory when not found in PATH; \"-isysroot\" and \"-Wl,-syslibroot\" can pass a regular file on disk to GNU ld.bfd, which interprets it as a positional linker script; and \"-x\" permitted specifying arbitrary compiler input languages beyond those supported by cgo. \"--sysroot\" and \"-target\" are now disallowed in \"#cgo\" flags, \"-isysroot\" and \"-Wl,-syslibroot\" are verified not to point to regular files, and \"-x\" is restricted to the C, C++, Objective-C, and assembler languages supported by cgo.",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
      "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"
    }
